[{"id": "R013", "text": "i rub my palm and take two deliberate breaths. i put one scrap aside, then take two cuts to see whether the pieces are identical or just rearranged leftovers. if they are identical, i leave them alone and leave the offcuts for the machine to clean."}, {"id": "R014", "text": "I mark both scraps with grease and leave them together side by side. I press one with a knuckle, then leave the other untouched. I run one short motion, then leave both alone for one minute. If they match, I mark again."}, {"id": "R015", "text": "i hold the two pieces together and then move the one with the edge. “i did not,” i say, then stop. the edge is worn, but the scrap remains. i keep it for now, though i do not trust the maker."}, {"id": "R016", "text": "“One piece,” I say, though the other looks like it belongs in the drawer. I pull both together, then stop dead."}, {"id": "R017", "text": "I touch the first piece and leave it where I put it. I tap the bench once and tap the second. I set them on the bench and turn the third once."}, {"id": "R018", "text": "I keep the smaller piece beside the bench. I tap it with my heel, then leave the larger one tucked under the bench. I fold the shorter one in half and leave it on the shelf. I keep the shorter one tucked against the bench’s edge."}, {"id": "R019", "text": "i touch the scraps first. “same,” i say. i leave them on the bench and move one piece closer. “not identical,” i say. i stop before the third piece. “not the same,” i say."}, {"id": "R020", "text": "Two pieces. I scrape one edge once, then turn it back. \"I leave it alone,\" I say. I scrape another scrap, then turn it back again. \"I say the same thing. I mark the edge.\" I mark the piece I leave alone."}, {"id": "R021", "text": "i put the scrap with the paper next to the offcut. it fits. i leave the paper beside it. the piece with the cut stays. i put a folded scrap on the bench beside it, not the one."}, {"id": "R022", "text": "i write the two pieces on the bench, then check the scrap. i leave both on the bench, then check the model. i leave the one with the more obvious match. i write the exact size on the scrap, then leave both alone."}, {"id": "R023", "text": "I touch the pieces. One is cut. I put it back. The scraps are gone. I leave one piece. I write the two pieces together. I keep the scraps. I keep the bench."}, {"id": "R024", "text": "1. check the pieces. 2. one small mark. 3. check the fold. 4. check the watch. slow. 5. one small square. 6. ask the other. 7. check the scrap. 8. i keep it tidy."}]
